  "oral_argument": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0002"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 4
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Scalia asked: \u201cWhat separates a stereotype from a reality? \u2026 is it not true that if there is an illegitimate child, it is much more likely that the woman will end up caring for it than the father?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0004"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 19,
              "start": 19
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Chief Justice Roberts, chief Justice Roberts stated: \u201cThe remedy for an equal protection violation is to treat everybody the same.\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3582b5486727-0001-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 21,
              "start": 21
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice Scalia, justice Scalia followed up with the question: \u201cUnless he\u2019s a United States citizen?\u201d"
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3582b5486727-0001-0006"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 34,
              "start": 34
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Justice Ginsburg asked whether giving fathers a one\u2011year advantage would be compatible with equal protection."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Justice BREYER",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3582b5486727-0002-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 39,
              "start": 39
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Justice BREYER, justice Breyer questioned the rationale for treating women worse than men in this context."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Chief Justice ROBERTS",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3582b5486727-0002-0003"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 48,
              "start": 48
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "Chief Justice Roberts asked whether the only possible remedy would be to increase the burden on mothers rather than relieve fathers."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Oral Argument",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "overview": {
    "claims": [
      {
        "attribution": "Court",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0000"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 3,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "In Nguyen, the Court approved a legitimation requirement only for fathers of non\u2011marital children born abroad, based on biological differences between men and women."
      },
      {
        "attribution": "Petitioner",
        "citations": [
          {
            "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
            "evidence_ids": [
              "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0001"
            ],
            "pages": {
              "end": 4,
              "start": 3
            }
          }
        ],
        "text": "According to Petitioner, the residential requirements at issue have no biological basis; they create barriers for younger fathers but not younger mothers and are rooted in gender stereotypes that assume women would care for non\u2011marital children."
      }
    ],
    "heading": "Overview",
    "status": "complete",
    "summary": null,
    "summary_citations": []
  },
  "party_positions": [
    {
      "claims": [
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3582b5486727-0000-0001"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 4,
                "start": 3
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Petitioner, the residential requirements are based on gender stereotypes and lack any biological justification, thus violating equal protection."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Petitioner",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "3582b5486727c8536ee8e3ad37b52fa12ec3eefc8ad1d60d3ce22db130f7c813",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-3582b5486727-0002-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 40,
                "start": 40
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "Congress intentionally made the rule tougher for fathers by balancing the duration of the parental connection, which the petitioner argues is unfair."
        }
      ],
      "heading": "Petitioner Position",
      "status": "complete",
      "summary": null,
      "summary_citations": []
    },
    {
      "claims": [
        {
